<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Hugh O'Donnell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1572–1602</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Hugh Roe O'Donnell</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Red Hugh O'Donnell was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">Tír Chonaill</a> in north-west Ireland. Imprisoned by the English in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin-castle">Dublin Castle</a> as a youth, he escaped in 1591 and became chief of the O'Donnells. With Hugh O'Neill he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>. After their defeat at Kinsale in 1601 he sailed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> for help and died there in 1602.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell.jpg" alt="Red Hugh O'Donnell" width="320" height="519" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard King · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugh_Roe_O%27Donnell,_depiction_in_stained-glass_window_by_Richard_King_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
